The provided test creates two owners in the same household (same lastName + postcode) and expects both to be created. The codebase already documents the intended mechanism for that — `EnsureUniqueHousehold` lets a request "opt in with `sharesHousehold` true ... as a declared household member." The test wasn't using it, so the second create was hitting the pre-existing 409 duplicate-household rule before the cap could ever be exercised. I added `b.put("sharesHousehold", true)` so the second owner is a declared household member, rather than gutting the existing uniqueness rule. Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).
